course: dictionary
lesson: 6149
title: The millimetre
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A millimetre is a very small length. It is written mm. Think of it as one tiny step on a ruler: ten millimetres make one centimetre, and a thousand make one metre.
explain: Look for the small lines between the centimetre numbers on a ruler. Each gap is one millimetre. «A centimetre is 10 millimetres» is a useful fact to remember when you change units.
explain: Scientists and engineers use millimetres for small lengths. «The UK minimum tread depth for cars is 1.6 millimetres.» Rain is measured in millimetres too, so a rain gauge can show how much rain has fallen.
fact: A millimetre is written mm.
fact: There are 10 millimetres in a centimetre and 1,000 millimetres in a metre.
fact: «A metre is 100 centimetres, and a centimetre is 10 millimetres.»
fact: «A frog from Papua New Guinea about seven millimetres long» is one of the smallest animals with a backbone.
fact: «A desert gets less than about 250 millimetres of rain a year.»
exercise: How many millimetres are in one centimetre? | 100 | 5 | 1,000 | *10
exercise: What is the short way to write millimetre? | *mm | ml | km | cm
exercise: How many millimetres make one metre? | 100 | 10,000 | 10 | *1,000
test: «The grooves in a tyre's tread push water away.» Which unit would you use to measure the tread depth on a car tyre? | metres | *millimetres | kilometres | litres
test: «Mountains still rise a few millimetres a year.» Which is the smallest length in this list? | 1 metre | 1 centimetre | *1 millimetre | 1 kilometre
exam: 250 millimetres is the same as how many centimetres? | *25 | 2.5 | 2,500 | 250
